course: dictionary
lesson: 13170
title: Foxy: sly, or like a fox
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word foxy can mean sly and clever at tricking people, or it can mean like a fox in looks, colour or smell. The words around it give you the clues. «The fox gave a foxy grin as it hid the stolen hen.» A grin is a face, and the hen was stolen, so foxy must mean sly and tricky here.
explain: «Her hair was a foxy red in the sunshine.» Red tells you the colour is the important part. Foxy means like a fox, so this is a reddish-brown colour, the colour of a fox's coat. Always ask: what does the sentence want the word to tell me? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Fables and stories often use the fox as a cunning character, such as Mr Fox or Reynard. That is why a «foxy» character is usually clever and sly. Ask yourself which meaning fits the rest of the sentence, and you will usually find the answer.
fact: Foxy means sly and clever at tricking people.
fact: Foxy can also mean like a fox in looks, colour or smell.
fact: «A foxy grin» is a sly, clever smile, as if someone is up to something.
fact: «Foxy red» means a reddish-brown colour, like a fox's coat.
fact: In fables, the fox is often cunning, so a foxy character is usually clever and sly.
exercise: «The fox gave a foxy grin as it hid the stolen hen.» What does foxy mean here? | *Sly and clever at tricking people | Happy and sleepy after a big meal | Loud and noisy in the field | Wet and cold from the rain
exercise: «Her hair was a foxy red in the sunshine.» What does foxy mean here? | *Like a fox in colour, reddish-brown | Dark blue, like the night sky | Soft and fluffy, like a cloud | Tall and thin, like a tree
exercise: «The foxy plan worked, and the hens were none the wiser.» Find and copy the word that tells you the plan was sly. | *foxy | plan | worked | hens
test: «The foxy smell drifted across the field.» What does foxy mean here? | Cold, like snow on the hill | *Like a fox, with a wild, animal smell | Sweet, like flowers in spring | Fresh, like rain on the grass
test: Why might a story call a character foxy? | Because they are very tall and strong | Because they can swim very fast | *Because they are sly and clever at tricking others | Because they like cold, snowy weather
exam: Which sentence uses foxy to mean reddish-brown? | «The foxy plan fooled everyone in the village.» | «He gave a foxy wink to his friend.» | «The foxy sly fox crept past the gate.» | *«Her foxy red hair shone in the sun.»
